; pipeline.eval — every source of damage in the game, through the one-pipeline
; check (Game/DamageLedger.h, docs/effects.md).
;
; THIS SUITE IS NOT LIKE THE OTHERS. The nine eval suites beside it MEASURE — a
; table to compare across knob changes, with no notion of a right answer. This
; one guards a RULE: outside the fx::ITarget adapters, nothing writes health.
; So it has a verdict, it lives in CheckAll's tier alongside the other checked
; rules, and tools\PipelineTest.ps1 reads its numbers rather than a human doing it.
;
; WHAT IT HAS TO DO IS FIRE EVERY ROUTE. A run that exercises three damage
; sources and reports PASS says nothing about the other nine — it is the same
; shape of empty pass the harness has produced twice before (a fresh party never
; runs the regeneration path; a reset check that prints no map geometry passes on
; a wrecked map). So the `pipeline` readout below prints per-route TOTALS, and
; PipelineTest.ps1 fails a run in which the pipeline route moved NOTHING. A check
; that ran no damage cannot report that damage behaved.
;
; DELIBERATELY NOT COVERED, and said out loud rather than left to be discovered:
; a PIT FALL. It is the one collision that needs a pit to fall down, arenas carve
; no stairs, and teleporting onto the showcase's pit mid-suite would take the
; party to another level and end the run. OnFallImpact shares CollideParty with
; the wall bump, which IS covered below, so the pipeline seam is exercised even
; though that entry point is not.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11

; Arm, then zero. `pipelineguard on` takes a fresh baseline (so arming can never
; manufacture a violation out of whatever happened before it) and `reset` clears
; the counters, so the totals below belong to this suite and not to the one that
; ran before it in the same process.
pipelineguard on
pipelineguard reset

; --- 1. THE DUNGEON AS A TARGET -------------------------------------------
; First, because it is the only section that needs the AUTHORED level: `reset`
; leaves showcase intact, and an arena strips every prop, door and fixture out of
; the map. All three breakable kinds are here, which is the point — the ledger
; watches decorations, doors and fixtures separately and each has its own adapter
; call to account for.
echo === 1. breakables: a prop, a door and a fixture ===
smash 10 12 6   ; the barrel   (Decoration)
smash 17 12 6   ; the crate    (Decoration)
smash 13 19 9   ; the wooden door AND the sconce sharing that cell
step 2
pipeline

; --- 2. MELEE, BOTH WAYS --------------------------------------------------
; A real encounter: the party swings (PartyTarget on the monster) and the monster
; swings back (MonsterTarget on a member). Two routes, one fight.
arena open 9 9
heal
tp 14 14
face north
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south
autoattack on
step 25
autoattack off
echo === 2. melee, both ways ===
party
monsters
pipeline

; --- 3. A BOLT, THROUGH THE PROJECTILE ENGINE -----------------------------
; The carrier path: a cast spawns a ProjectileSpec, which lands a DamageEvent
; through the same adapters. Tilo (member 3) is the caster with mana.
arena corridor 11
heal
tp 10 12
face east
spawn skel_warrior 16 12 west
freeze on
learn 3 fire
cast 3 fire
cast 3 fire
step 8
echo === 3. a bolt in flight ===
monsters
pipeline

; --- 4. AN AREA BLAST -----------------------------------------------------
; A blast has no side and reaches several targets at once; every square it fills
; is a separate Deal. The party is teleported clear — their deaths are not what
; is being checked.
arena tjunction 9 5
; 10,12 — INSIDE the bar. A tp to a cell outside the arena is REFUSED and leaves
; the party where the carve put them, which is the centre: ground zero. The first
; run of this suite said `tp 20 12`, wiped the party on the junction's x6
; convergence, and then reported PASS for four more sections while nothing
; simulated at all. Every section below now opens with `heal` for the same reason.
tp 10 12
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south
blast fireburst 14 12
step 6
echo === 4. a blast at a junction ===
monsters
pipeline

; --- 5. DoTs ON BOTH SIDES, AND A WARD'S REPRISAL -------------------------
; A DoT bites as a Tick through Deal, resisted as it goes; a fire shield answers
; a blow with a Burst that is itself deflected, absorbed and resisted like any
; other damage. The reprisal is the subtle one — it used to do its own
; arithmetic, and putting it through the pipeline is what let a fire-eating
; monster be FED by punching a fire shield.
arena open 9 9
heal
tp 14 14
face north
freeze off
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south
effect burn 0 4 8          ; a member burns
effect burn ahead 4 8      ; ...and so does the monster
effect fireshield 0 6 30   ; and hitting that member costs the monster
step 25
echo === 5. DoTs both ways, and a reprisal ===
party
monsters
pipeline

; --- 6. THE WORLD'S OWN BLOW: A WALL BUMP ---------------------------------
; Impact damage, shared with the pit landing (CollideParty). Walking into rock
; is the reachable half of that pair.
arena corridor 11
heal
tp 10 12
face west
forward 4
step 6
echo === 6. walked into a wall ===
party
pipeline

; --- 7. OVER-EXERTION: THE DECLARED EXCEPTION ------------------------------
; The one route that reaches health WITHOUT building a DamageEvent (Michael's
; call, 2026-08-15): exhaustion is not resisted, soaked or warded. It is named in
; the ledger rather than quietly permitted, so it shows in the readout as its own
; row — and a day when it moves to the pipeline, that row goes to zero and this
; comment is what says the change was deliberate.
;
; A stance past 1 is what buys the points that get billed, and the bill only
; reaches HEALTH once stamina is gone, so the bar is emptied first by swinging.
heal
tp 14 14
face north
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south
; A TRAINED fighter, because an untrained one cannot over-exert at all: the
; points a stance past 1 buys scale with the skill curve, so recklessness is a
; veteran's option (docs/damage-system.md). The first version of this section
; put a novice Brand at share 2.0, swung fourteen times, and billed nothing —
; the `exertion` row stayed at zero and the declared exception went unexercised.
setskill 0 unarmed 12
guard 2 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
step 4
echo === 7. over-exertion ===
party
pipeline

; --- 8. COMING ROUND BY YOURSELF ------------------------------------------
; The one route where health goes UP for a reason no effect owns: an unconscious
; member accrues safe seconds and wakes at stabilize_health (docs/combat.md
; Phase 5). Over-exertion above is the clean way to get someone there — it can
; empty the bar and by design can never kill — and the arena clears the monster
; whose presence would otherwise keep resetting the safe-seconds clock. NO heal
; here, obviously: healing him is the one thing that would stop this measuring.
arena open 9 9
step 40
echo === 8. woke up by himself ===
party
pipeline

; --- 9. STARVATION: A METER'S SHADOW BITING -------------------------------
; An emptied food meter raises `starving`, which ticks damage like any other DoT.
; docs/health-and-healing.md bought "starvation can kill you" from the overkill
; rule rather than writing a death path, and this is the seam that makes that
; true: it arrives as a Tick through Deal.
heal
setsupply 0 food 0
setsupply 0 water 0
step 20
echo === 9. starving ===
party
supplies

; --- the verdict ----------------------------------------------------------
; PipelineTest.ps1 reads the RESULT= line, and reads the per-route totals to
; confirm the suite actually ran damage rather than passing by doing nothing.
echo === one-pipeline check ===
pipeline
state
